<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yellow Turban Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/184">184 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yellow Turban Rebellion was a large peasant uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> that began in 184 CE, led by the Taoist faith healer Zhang Jue and his brothers. Driven by millenarian expectations and agrarian distress, it spread across much of northern China. Although suppressed, it greatly strengthened regional warlords, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> treat it as a major step towards the dynasty's collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yellow-turban-rebellion.jpg" alt="Yellow Turban Rebellion" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellow_Turban_Rebellion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Yellow Turban Rebellion</b> of 184 CE, a millenarian Taoist uprising fed by decades of peasant displacement and famine, forced the court to delegate military authority to regional commanders whose loyalty was personal rather than institutional.</blockquote><a href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The collapse of Han authority after the <b>Yellow Turban</b> rebellion of 184 left the frontier in turmoil, and several Xianbei leaders competed for power, among them Budugen, a member of Tanshihuai's family, and Kebineng.</blockquote><a href="/empire/xianbei">Xianbei · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Sun Ce, son of Sun Jian, a general against the <b>Yellow Turbans</b>, conquered the region south of the Yangtze in the 190s.</blockquote><a href="/state/eastern-wu">Eastern Wu</a></li><li><blockquote>Their cavalry fought for the Han against the Northern Xiongnu and later in the <b>Yellow Turban</b> wars.</blockquote><a href="/state/southern-xiongnu">Southern Xiongnu</a></li></ul></section>
